    {
      "chunk_id": "ver_d449b1cc14cf_c00001",
      "document_id": "doc_owasp_a03_query_parameterization_cheat_sheet",
      "version_id": "ver_d449b1cc14cf",
      "chunk_idx": 1,
      "chunk_type": "heading",
      "text_content": "## Introduction",
      "token_count": 3,
      "chunk_strategy": "structure_aware",
      "heading_path": [
        "Query Parameterization Cheat Sheet",
        "Introduction"
      ]
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ver_d449b1cc14cf_c00002",
      "document_id": "doc_owasp_a03_query_parameterization_cheat_sheet",
      "version_id": "ver_d449b1cc14cf",
      "chunk_idx": 2,
      "chunk_type": "paragraph",
      "text_content": "[SQL Injection](https://owasp.org/www-community/attacks/SQL_Injection) is one of the most dangerous web vulnerabilities.\n\nAs of the [OWASP Top 10:2025](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/), it is categorized under A05:2025-Injection.\n\nIt represents a serious threat because SQL Injection allows evil attacker code to change the structure of a web application's SQL statement in a way that can steal data, modify data, or potentially facilitate command injection to the underlying OS.\n\nThis cheat sheet is a derivative work of the [SQL Injection Prevention Cheat Sheet](SQL_Injection_Prevention_Cheat_Sheet.md).",
      "token_count": 136,
      "chunk_strategy": "structure_aware",
      "heading_path": [
        "Query Parameterization Cheat Sheet",
        "Introduction"
      ]
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ver_d449b1cc14cf_c00003",
      "document_id": "doc_owasp_a03_query_parameterization_cheat_sheet",
      "version_id": "ver_d449b1cc14cf",
      "chunk_idx": 3,
      "chunk_type": "heading",
      "text_content": "## Parameterized Query Examples",
      "token_count": 5,
      "chunk_strategy": "structure_aware",
      "heading_path": [
        "Query Parameterization Cheat Sheet",
        "Parameterized Query Examples"
      ]
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ver_d449b1cc14cf_c00004",
      "document_id": "doc_owasp_a03_query_parameterization_cheat_sheet",
      "version_id": "ver_d449b1cc14cf",
      "chunk_idx": 4,
      "chunk_type": "paragraph",
      "text_content": "SQL Injection is best prevented through the use of [*parameterized queries*](SQL_Injection_Prevention_Cheat_Sheet.md).\n\nThe following chart demonstrates, with real-world code samples, how to build parameterized queries in most of the common web languages.\n\nThe purpose of these code samples is to demonstrate to the web developer how to avoid SQL Injection when building database queries within a web application.\n\nPlease note, many client side frameworks and libraries offer client side query parameterization.\n\nThese libraries often just build queries with string concatenation before sending raw queries to a server.\n\nPlease ensure that query parameterization is done server-side!",
      "token_count": 116,
      "chunk_strategy": "structure_aware",
      "heading_path": [
        "Query Parameterization Cheat Sheet",
        "Parameterized Query Examples"
      ]
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ver_d449b1cc14cf_c00005",
      "document_id": "doc_owasp_a03_query_parameterization_cheat_sheet",
      "version_id": "ver_d449b1cc14cf",
      "chunk_idx": 5,
      "chunk_type": "heading",
      "text_content": "### Prepared Statement Examples",
      "token_count": 6,
      "chunk_strategy": "structure_aware",
      "heading_path": [
        "Query Parameterization Cheat Sheet",
        "Parameterized Query Examples",
        "Prepared Statement Examples"
      ]
    },
    {
